Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.35,0:00:05.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,In a home for the elderly, two\Nold men shared one room.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.11,0:00:07.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,The room had a single window.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.56,0:00:11.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ato Girma’s bed was beside it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.17,0:00:16.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ato Kebede lay flat on his\Nback and saw only the ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.06,0:00:22.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every afternoon, Ato Girma sat\Nup and described everything he
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.38,0:00:25.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,could see through the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.85,0:00:30.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,“I see a garden ringed with\Nbeautiful trees…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.19,0:00:32.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,children chasing a ball.”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.56,0:00:36.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,“Sweethearts walk hand in\Nhand…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.61,0:00:40.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,and beyond them, I see lovely\Nhills.”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.18,0:00:45.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ato Kebede closed his eyes and\Nsaw it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.21,0:00:47.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Weeks went by like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.43,0:00:51.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,One morning, Ato Girma’s bed\Nwas empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.09,0:00:53.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,He had passed away in the\Nnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.18,0:00:58.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ato Kebede asked for his bed\Nto be moved to the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.26,0:01:00.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,He could not wait to see.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.02,0:01:05.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,But beyond the window there\Nwas only a white wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.68,0:01:10.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,The caregiver told him, “Ato\NGirma could not see.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.32,0:01:11.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,He was blind.”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.56,0:01:16.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,He had invented it all, to\Ngive his friend the hope to go
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.77,0:01:17.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,on living.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.08,0:01:21.08,Card,,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,0)}{\fs88\b1}The Window{\b0\fs59}\N\NMade with AI
